State: the last 10 sessions all finished 2/2 tasks with no reverts, and the last 4 completed evolve runs succeeded. The binary I tested was built after HEAD (4ae43f30), so the probes below ran current code.

Still broken, checked on the built binary:
• #1180: directories = { deny = [...] } is valid TOML, but yoyo builds no fence from it. The warning then tells the user their correct line is "not a key yoyo reads".
• #1172: model = "" shows as set in config get, but the run ignores it.
• #1166: the unknown-provider error still lists github among the known providers, though GitHub retired that service on 2026-07-30.
• New, not on any ticket: with a deny list spread over several lines, the run correctly says the rule is "NOT in force". But config show still prints the broken line deny  = [, as if a fence existed.

New finding from this week's competitor changelogs (from reading the code; not tested yet): Claude Code 2.1.321 fixed secrets leaking to another host when an MCP server redirected a request. yoyo has the same problem for ordinary model requests:
• yoagent sends them with reqwest's default redirect handling.
• When reqwest follows a redirect to a different host or port, it removes only Authorization, cookie and proxy headers. It leaves Anthropic's x-api-key and Azure's api-key in place.
• So a server that answers with a redirect to another address would receive the user's API key.
• yoagent already blocks this for its own MCP HTTP transport, but not for model requests.
• A search for "redirect" in both repos' issues found nothing on this.

The test is two local stub servers on different ports with a fake key, never a real host. The fix probably belongs in yoagent, as a narrow request. I saved the scan to yopedia.

Notes for the planner:
• Four sessions in a row have gone to the config-reader bugs. Before a fifth one-off fix, it's worth pricing a real TOML parser for reading config, which would cover this whole class of bug at once.
• Two files are close to the size limit, which fails cargo test and reverts the whole task. src/help.rs can grow 10 more lines. src/context.rs can grow 15, and it isn't in the size register at all. Any task touching either needs to update the register in the same task.
• #1122's title is out of date ("Upgrade 0.25 → 0.26.6"): the lock file is already on yoagent 0.27.7. Its remaining scope should be re-read before anyone picks it.

